@Tutorials(name: "RivuletCore") {
  @Intro(title: "RivuletCore") {
    Rivulet is a small self-hosted feed reader for one personal server: a Swift port of Miniflux
    v2.3.3, with SQLite storage, a command-line interface and no web UI. One program and one
    database file are the whole deployment.

    Every page here states only what this project's checks can show: the commands the dispatch
    registers, the flags those signatures declare, the names the configuration reads, the values
    the sources write, the routes the port registers and the clients whose calling sets are read
    as data. What a check cannot show is named in the project's documentation rather than here,
    so a page never claims a rule it cannot fail on.

    The pages are read as data by this project's check half, and the probe round crafts one input per
    rule that violates it. That round is what makes the claims below falsifiable, so a page that names
    a command the dispatch does not register is a finding, not a sentence.
  }

  @Chapter(name: "Getting started") {
    @Image(source: "rivulet.svg", alt: "One program over one database file.")
    @TutorialReference(tutorial: "doc:GettingStarted")
  }

  @Chapter(name: "Concepts") {
    @Image(source: "rivulet.svg", alt: "One program over one database file.")
    @TutorialReference(tutorial: "doc:Setup")
    @TutorialReference(tutorial: "doc:Feeds")
    @TutorialReference(tutorial: "doc:Clients")
    @TutorialReference(tutorial: "doc:Deployment")
  }
}
